  "question": {
    "text": "The number of electrons involved in the reduction of permanganate to manganese dioxide in acidic medium is _____ .",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Permanganate is reduced to Manganese dioxide by the following reaction:<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><msubsup><mi>MnO</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>&#10230;</mo><mover><mi>Mn</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mover><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math><br />Here, oxidation no. of manganese was reduced by 3 from reactant to product side. Thus, three electrons are involved.",
